@title A letter about our Elm Street shop
@author Marguerite Pell, Owner, Corbel & Finch Books

Dear friends,

We have hard news to share, and we would rather you hear it from us.

## What is changing

Our Elm Street shop, open for 17 years, will close for good after we trade on 2026-12-23.

We know many of you have been coming through that door for most of those years. So have we. It is not an easy thing to write.

## Why

Two things led us here.

- The Elm Street rent will rise 70% when the lease renews on 2027-01-01.
- More than half of our sales now happen at Harbor Road or online.

So the family chose to keep the two places that are growing. We wish the numbers had let us keep all three.

## What stays the same

- The Harbor Road shop, the online shop and the school book fairs all continue.
- Our team of 6 Elm Street booksellers will move to Harbor Road. The faces will be the same.
- Gift certificates and store credit are honored at Harbor Road and online until 2027-12-31.
- Loyalty points move over automatically. There is nothing for you to do.

## How to say goodbye

We would love to see you before we close.

step All Elm Street stock is 20% off | from 2026-11-28
step Last Saturday story hour, at 11:00 | 2026-12-19
step Farewell evening with the staff and local authors, 17:00 to 20:00 | 2026-12-22
step Final day of trading at Elm Street | 2026-12-23

Thank you, truly, for 17 years of stories, recommendations and kindness. You made this shop what it was.

With gratitude,

Marguerite Pell
